@model ReformedHistory.Views.Content.Confessions.Secret.SecretSection

<h2 id="@this.Model.Link">Chapter @this.Model.Index</h2>
<h3>@this.Model.Name</h3>
<br />

<div class="centerQuote">
    <span>
        It is therefore apparent what difference there is between the old covenant and the new: 
        In the former the law is written on tables, while in the latter on hearts; the 
        one alarms from without, but the other delights from within. In the former man becomes a transgressor 
        through the letter that kills, in the other a lover through the life-giving Spirit.
    </span>
    <span>Saint Augustine, On the Spirit and the Letter</span>
</div>
    
<ol>
    <li>
        The old covenant under Moses was good, but it could not fulfill God's promises to Israel to save them from
        their sins and to make them a holy nation. 
    </li>
    <li>
        A new and better covenant was needed, which was foretold by the prophets Jeremiah, Ezekiel, Isaiah, and
        others. The new covenant would not be like the old, where God's people had to be taught to know the Lord
        through the law. Instead God would write the law on their hearts and put His Spirit within them, so that
        they would all know God. God would forgive their sins and remember their transgressions no more.

        @*<div class="centerQuote">
            <span>
